A particle of mass $M$ at $vb(x_0)$ attracts a particle of mass $m$ at $vb(x)$ through the potential $V = -(G M m)/(abs(vb(x) - vb(x_0)))$, giving the inverse square law $vb(F) = - (G M m)/(r^2) vu(r)$ for $vb(r) = vb(x) - vb(x_0)$, with $G$ approximately $6.67 times 10^(-11)$ $"m"^3 "kg"^(-1) "s"^(-2)$.
